DNS Hierarchy for www.google.com:

1. Root (.):
   - The highest level in DNS hierarchy represented by the invisible dot at the end (www.google.com.). It directs queries to top-level domain servers.

2. TLD (Top-Level Domain):
   - The main extension after the domain name. In "www.google.com", ".com" is the TLD.

3. Domain:
   - The registered unique brand/organization name. In "www.google.com", "google" is the domain name.

4. Subdomain:
   - The specific prefix that precedes the root domain name. In "www.google.com", "www" is the subdomain.
